// A tree whose children are in an order (Inputs/tree_order.ent): a `for`
// that cascades visits the children of a node by their slots, and in the
// order they were connected where those are the same; a binding `before`
// the tree is the sibling before, and with `optional` the `for` also
// visits the first of them, and the root, which has no parent either.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_order.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tree_order.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// Connected a, b, c with slots 2, 1, 3: b (20 wide) first, then a (10),
// then c.
// CHECK:      1: root 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a 120
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: c 130
// Under b, both with slot 0 (one has none): the one connected first.
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b2 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b1 102
// c is given slot 0: it is first, and all after it start 30 later.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: root 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: c 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: b 130
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: a 150
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: b2 130
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: b1 132
// A new node with a's slot comes after a, and before nothing.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: c 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b 130
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a 150
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: d 160
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b2 130
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b1 132
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
